+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Every tool declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is handed verbatim to the providers, and `ToolRegistry.execute` checks the model's input against that schema before the executor runs. A malformed call becomes a tool result the model can read and correct within the tool-round budget, rather than reaching the executor or ending the conversation with a transport error.
+
+## Rejecting input the schema refuses
+
+- Input missing a `required` property is answered with a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: rejects input missing a required field as a result naming it, without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L39)).
+- A rejection names the failing property path and the constraint that failed, and never a property value, in the returned result or in any log line ([validated by: names the failing path and expected type but never a value, in the result or any log line](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L49)).
+- A rejection is a tool result, not an exception: `processMessage` resolves, the rejection text is what the provider sees on the next round, and the tool-round bound is what stops a retry cycle from spinning ([validated by: feeds a rejected tool call back to the model, which retries and the message resolves](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L51)).
+
+## Compiling schemas
+
+- A static tool's schema is compiled at `register` time, so an uncompilable schema throws there with a message naming the tool, rather than failing mid-conversation ([validated by: throws at register time for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
+- A function-valued definition is resolved per call and validated against the schema current at that call, never a stale cached one ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at that call, not a stale one](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L87)).
+
+## What validation does not do
+
+Validation enforces `required`, declared types and `enum` only. It does not inject `additionalProperties: false`, coerce types or apply defaults, so valid input with unlisted extra properties reaches the executor unchanged. There is no opt-out flag. `execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` for an unregistered name; returning that to the model instead is a separate issue.
